    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d990-a4">

                <pb facs="0755" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg639"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]<anchor n="78" xml:id="d990-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-24T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view [etc. as in next above] departure. When you decide to leave, close the
                    consular office and transfer archives with coats of arms, flags and seals to
                    safe place in United States, taking with you the code, current accounts and fee
                    stamps. Procure vouchers for transportation expenses of your family and instruct
                    members of your staff to do likewise. Will keep you advised as far as possible
                    of general situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d990-f1" n="78" xml:id="d990-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Matamoros, Juárez, Díaz and Nuevo Laredo; same to Nogales, adding:
                    “Endeavor to communicate foregoing to Cananea, directing Agent to close office
                    and securely store archives, coats of arms, flags and seals.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
